  "notes": [
    "The GT dataset does not store raw control/treatment means - it stores pre-computed effect sizes: (E-A)/A and ln(r). Numeric matching must use ln_rr from extraction vs ln(r) from GT.",
    "The GT 'Reference' column appears to contain author+year strings used as study identifiers.",
    "The extraction field 'ln_rr' corresponds to GT 'ln(r)'; extraction 'effect_pct' corresponds to GT '(E-A)/A' (as a proportion, not percentage - GT range is -0.77 to 2.09 while extraction effect_pct range is -93.9 to 750, suggesting GT uses ratio form while extraction uses percent).",
    "GT '(E-A)/A' is a proportion (e.g., -0.77 means -77%), while extraction 'effect_pct' appears to be in percent (e.g., -77). A factor of 0.01 converts extraction effect_pct to GT (E-A)/A scale.",
    "Match constraints should include Element (from GT) vs element (from extraction) and Tissue (from GT) vs tissue (from extraction).",
    "The GT dataset has 27 elements including Ca, Fe, K, Mg, Mn, N, P, C, Na, Zn, B, Cu, S, Al, Ba, Cd, Mo, Ni, Pb, Se, Cr, Br, Co, Si, V, Sr, Cl.",
    "The extraction data contains many non-mineral outcomes (biomass, growth, photosynthesis, etc.) that must be filtered out before matching to GT mineral concentration data.",
    "Some extraction papers (e.g., 005_Niinemets_1999, 028_Mishra_2011, 051_Niu_2013) contain mixed outcomes including non-mineral measurements (SPAD, conductance, etc.) that should be excluded.",
    "Unit diversity in extraction is high (%, mg/g, mg/kg, g/kg, ppm, etc.) but since GT only stores effect sizes (not raw means), unit alignment is less critical for matching - the ln(r) is dimensionless.",
    "The 'n' field in GT appears to be sample size per observation (values: 2-48), matching extraction 'n' field.",
    "Paper 037_de_2000 likely corresponds to 'de Groot 2000' or similar - the 'de' prefix suggests a Dutch/German surname.",
    "Paper 058_ONeill_1987 corresponds to O'Neill 1987.",
    "The GT has a 'Study Type' column (glasshouse, FACE, OTC, chamber, tunnel-chamber, greenhouse, tunnel) that matches extraction moderators.",
    "Extraction observations with non-mineral outcomes (yield, biomass, dry weight, photosynthesis, water use, growth) must be excluded via ext_exclude_keywords."
  ],
